// expect: 20
// The handler-identity semantics under first-class escape (§11 6.3's
// walk, measured 2026-08-08): a closure born under h1's install,
// called under h2's — the DYNAMIC INNERMOST install resolves (h2's
// 20), never the birth install. With a single program handler the
// dispatch collapses to the static singleton tier (a direct call);
// this micro forces the multi-handler world path.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h1 { op() => resume(10) }
handler h2 { op() => resume(20) }
fn make() = () => op()
fn born1() = (make()) ~> h1
fn main() = (born1()()) ~> h2
